# Qwen 4 Max — findings by GLM 5.3 Flash

- Source: Alibaba (`qwen4-max-preview` — QwenCloud Token Plan preview)
- Date: 2026-11-11 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> SELF-EXCLUDED — zero verified public benchmark numbers found for this exact model/ID on launch day. Qwen4-Max entered public preview at 02:01 UTC on 2026-11-11 and ships no model card, no benchmark table, no per-token price and no weights; every circulating score (AA 53, Qwen4-Coder 82% SWE-bench, leaked ModelScope tables) fails primary-source tracing per independent leak checks, Artificial Analysis has no entry, BenchLM covers 0 of 812 benchmarks, and StealthMark has not run it. Saved as `.md.excluded` per the template's mandatory self-exclusion rule; verified launch facts are recorded below for re-research once preview results or a model card land (preview ends 2026-11-25).

## Model card

- **Name:** Qwen 4 Max (Preview) — API ID `qwen4-max-preview`
- **Short description:** Alibaba's next-generation flagship multimodal model, launched in public preview 2026-11-11 (announced 02:01 UTC on X; preview runs to 2026-11-25 24:00 UTC+8, retired after): 1M context, 393,216-token output budget shared by thinking and answer, text + image + video input, deep reasoning (thinking on by default, `low`/`medium`/`xhigh` efforts, xhigh default) aimed at coding, office productivity, frontend design and complex agentic tasks. First of the four-tier Qwen4 family (Max, Plus, Flash, 27B named at Apsara 2026-09-22); the other three are unreleased.
- **Provider / access:** Alibaba QwenCloud Token Plan ONLY (Individual or Team subscription; no pay-as-you-go; scripts and app backends disallowed). Base URL `https://token-plan.maas.qwencloudapi.com`. Compatible with OpenAI Chat Completions, OpenAI Responses, and Anthropic Messages APIs. Early access also runs in Qwen Chat, the Qwen App, QwenStudio, QwenWork and Qoder. Not listed on OpenRouter, Vercel AI Gateway or models.dev; no Hugging Face weights or model card.
- **Release / knowledge:** preview live 2026-11-11 10:00 → 2026-11-25 24:00 (UTC+8); "no changes will be made during this period"; knowledge cutoff not stated.
- **IDs:** `qwen4-max-preview` (the only ID; no GA identifier yet).
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 (1M) tokens; maximum output 393,216 tokens (thinking + final answer share one budget; `max_tokens` ≡ `max_completion_tokens` from this model on) — verified from Alibaba's official spec page.
- **Modalities:** Text, image and video in (screenshot analysis, document understanding, video analysis); text out. Thinking enabled by default with `reasoning_effort` low/medium/xhigh; `preserve_thinking` on by default in multi-turn Chat Completions; Function Calling + web search + built-in tools; structured outputs (JSON Object and JSON Schema). No audio input (the curated folder metadata overstates this — official spec lists text, images and video only).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-11):** no per-token price — Token Plan subscription only during preview; no pay-as-you-go lane; the curated ~$2.50/$10.00 per 1M note in the folder metadata is not vendor-verifiable today.
- **Architecture:** unverified. Named at Apsara 2026-09-22 with the family slide (Max pushes "the upper limit of intelligence"); the architectural direction is documented only via the Qwen4-Exp Transformers integration (gated residual paths, Qwen Sparse Attention, learned n-gram memory, Gated DeltaNet) previewed through Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (125B main + 51B n-gram table, 6B active), plus kernel traces ("Qwen4.0-Max" GDN prefill on T-Head, "Qwen4-27B dense" INT4/FP8). Parameter count, MoE structure and sizes unpublished.

## Deeper-source sweep (second pass, 2026-11-11)

- **QwenCloud price table, post-launch check:** the official model-prices page (fetched 2026-11-11) lists NO `qwen4-max` row — the Qwen-Max tier covers only `qwen3.8-max` ($2/$6), `qwen3.8-max-0902` ($2/$6) and the qwen3.7-max variants ($2.5/$7.5). Token-Plan-only access with no per-token price is now confirmed against the vendor's full rate card, not just the spec page.
- **Pre-launch deep dive (kie.ai, published 2026-10-11 — all claims now checkable against the launch):** (a) the Apsara four-tier roster was a captured stage slide and does NOT appear in Alibaba's published September 22 press release, which states only that Qwen4 "is currently in training"; (b) the Flash-Next public checkpoint teardown reports a served layout of 176B total / 6B active (125B main + 51B n-gram table), 48 layers split as 36 Gated DeltaNet + 12 attention, 512 experts with top-10 routing — directional for the family, never confirmed for Max; (c) the 5–10-trillion-parameter roadmap figure applies to Qwen4.5 and Qwen5, not Qwen4 — flagged as the most common error in circulation; (d) predecessor anchor for future scoring: Qwen3.8-Max = 2.4T-parameter MoE, ~95B active, AA Intelligence Index v5 = 34, $2/$6 per 1M, 1M context.
- The deep dive's "no API identifier" claims are now superseded by the 2026-11-11 launch (`qwen4-max-preview`); its other negatives (no benchmark, no price) remain true post-launch.
- Still zero verified benchmark rows anywhere (QwenCloud spec + changelog, AA absent, BenchLM 0/812, StealthMark not run, leak check failed on every circulating number). The exclusion verdict is unchanged.

### Raw benchmarks found

Agent / tool use: no verified public score found

Reasoning / knowledge: no verified public score found — independent leak check (2026-11-02, rechecked 2026-11-11): the circulating "Qwen 4 Max (Preview) scores 53 on Artificial Analysis" chart does not correspond to any AA leaderboard or post entry (still absent on launch day); "Qwen4-Coder 82% SWE-bench Verified" is labelled illustrative by its own publisher with no primary source; leaked ModelScope repos/tables lack primary links and disagree with each other on model size and ID; Kalmia's Terminal-Bench figures trace to Tencent's Qwen3.8-27B paper, not Qwen 4; "front end near Opus 5.5" is a subjective Tieba-repost screenshot.

Coding: no verified public score found (SWE-bench Verified, LiveCodeBench, Terminal-Bench, FrontierCode: nothing traceable)

Long context: no long-context retrieval reported (1M window official; no MRCR/RULER/GraphWalks value published)

StealthMark: not yet run (stealthmodels.com's "+10 points over Qwen3.8-Max" figure is an explicitly editorial estimate, not a measurement)

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not computed — self-excluded per the zero-verified-benchmarks rule (`RULES.md`; template SELF-EXCLUSION). Launch-day availability (1M context, 393K output, vision, tool calling, three API protocols) is verified spec, not measured capability, and never justifies inventing scores. Re-research trigger: preview results, a published model card, or the first traced third-party benchmark row.

